===Etymology===
* (''Zaltbommel'') First attested as ''in uilla halosta'' around 850. Etymology {{unc|nl|nocap=1}}. A proposed derivation from {{m|nl|els|t=alder, ''Alnus''}} with collectivising suffix ''-t'' does not match well with old attestations of the toponym. Potentially derived from {{inh|nl|gem-pro|*alhust|t=dwelling place, shrine}}. Compare {{m|nl|Elst}}, {{m|nl|Maasniel}}, {{m|nl|Nieuwaal}}, {{m|nl|Niel}}, {{m|nl|Niel-bij-As}}, {{m|nl|Nivele}} and {{m|de|Waldniel}}.
* (''Noord-Brabant'') First attested as ''alst'' in 1281. Etymology uncertain. The formerly widespread hypothesis of a derivation from {{m|nl|els|t=alder, ''Alnus''}} with collectivising suffix ''-t'' is no longer considered plausible. Potentially derived from {{inh|nl|gem-pro|*alhust|t=dwelling place, shrine}}. Compare {{m|nl|Elst}}, {{m|nl|Maasniel}}, {{m|nl|Nieuwaal}}, {{m|nl|Niel}}, {{m|nl|Niel-bij-As}}, {{m|nl|Nivele}} and {{m|de|Waldniel}}.
* (''Buren'') First attested as ''aelst'' around 1400. Etymology uncertain. A proposed derivation from {{m|nl|els|t=alder, ''Alnus''}} with collectivising suffix ''-t'' does not match well with old attestations of the toponym. Potentially derived from {{inh|nl|gem-pro|*alhust|t=dwelling place, shrine}}. Compare {{m|nl|Elst}}, {{m|nl|Maasniel}}, {{m|nl|Nieuwaal}}, {{m|nl|Niel}}, {{m|nl|Niel-bij-As}}, {{m|nl|Nivele}} and {{m|de|Waldniel}}.

